# Dale & Son — where the job information lives

This folder has no job files in it. Everything about the work lives in a
Postgres database — the well.

The connection string is in `.env.local` as `DATABASE_URL`. Never print
it, never paste it into a reply, and never write it into any other file.

## Asking the well a question

Run the SQL with psql:

```
psql "$env:DATABASE_URL" -c "<the SQL>"
```

**Always show me the SQL**, in a code block, before the answer. Then say
in one sentence what it asks for, in plain English. I want to be able to
check it says what I meant before I believe the numbers.

All money is US dollars. Write it as $1,104.50 — never any other
currency symbol.

## What is in the well

One table, `jobs`:

| column | what it holds |
|---|---|
| `customer` | surname, the way Dale says it |
| `address` | where the job is, if we know |
| `job` | one line describing the work |
| `status` | `ready to price`, `stopped`, or `sent` |
| `waiting_on` | who the ball is with, blank if nobody |
| `received` | the day the request came in |
| `total` | what it was billed at, blank until it is sent |

## House rules, same as always

Never price gas work — flag it for Dale and say why. Never promise a
date. Plain language; the customer is not a plumber.
